 I('openshell','NVIDIA OpenShell: policy outside the agent','https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/add-runtime-controls-to-ai-agents-with-nvidia-openshell/','NVIDIA OpenShell runtime controls','official technical blog','Published Sep 28; OpenShell 0.1.0','An open-source runtime wrapping Codex, Claude Code, Pi, or Hermes with kernel, network, credential, MCP, and audit controls.','It makes permissions enforceable even when the model generates shell commands, child processes, or delegated work.','Compare the supervisor/sandbox split with Hermes execution boundaries and build a policy-backed worker profile.',['Controls survive bad prompts','Credentials stay out of workloads','OCSF decisions become evidence'],'Treat 0.1.0 as an evaluation target, not a drop-in production control plane. Run one read-only sandbox test.','Runtime guardrails'),
